"title: Quickstart\n"
"description: A quickstart guide for the Shaded lightcones Qiskit addon (qiskit-addon-slc)\n"
msgstr ""
"title: Quickstart\n"
"description: Panduan quickstart untuk addon Qiskit Shaded lightcones (qiskit-addon-slc)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide demonstrates a minimal working example of the `qiskit-addon-slc` package. It calculates a shaded lightcone to reduce the sampling cost of probabilistic error cancellation (PEC).\n"
msgstr "Panduan ini menunjukkan contoh minimal yang berfungsi dari paket `qiskit-addon-slc`. Panduan ini menghitung shaded lightcone untuk mengurangi biaya sampling dari probabilistic error cancellation (PEC).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEC mitigates gate noise by sampling from a quasiprobability decomposition of the inverse noise channel. Its sampling cost grows with every error term it must mitigate; however, not every error affects the observable equally. An error outside the observable's causal lightcone cannot influence the measured expectation value, and even within the lightcone, some errors are more detrimental than others. A shaded lightcone quantifies this by bounding the effect each Pauli error term has on the observable. Truncating the error terms with the smallest effect shrinks the noise model that PEC has to mitigate, reducing sampling cost in exchange for a small, bounded bias.\n"
msgstr "PEC memitigasi noise gate dengan mensampel dari dekomposisi kuasiprobabilitas dari kanal noise invers. Biaya sampling-nya naik seiring setiap suku error yang harus dimitigasi; namun, tidak semua error memengaruhi observable secara setara. Error di luar lightcone kausal observable tidak bisa memengaruhi nilai ekspektasi yang terukur, dan bahkan di dalam lightcone pun, sebagian error lebih merusak daripada yang lain. Shaded lightcone mengkuantifikasi hal ini dengan membatasi pengaruh setiap suku error Pauli terhadap observable. Memangkas suku error dengan pengaruh terkecil akan mengecilkan model noise yang harus dimitigasi PEC, sehingga biaya sampling berkurang dengan imbalan bias kecil yang terbatas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To see how to build a realistic workflow and run on quantum hardware, check out the [Probabilistic error cancellation with shaded lightcones](/tutorials/pec-with-shaded-lightcones) tutorial on IBM Quantum Platform.\n"
msgstr "Untuk melihat cara membangun alur kerja yang realistis dan menjalankannya di hardware kuantum, lihat tutorial [Probabilistic error cancellation with shaded lightcones](/tutorials/pec-with-shaded-lightcones) di IBM Quantum Platform.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Prepare the inputs for SLC {#1-prepare-the-inputs-for-slc}"
msgstr "1. Siapkan input untuk SLC {#1-prepare-the-inputs-for-slc}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, build a 10-qubit Trotterized transverse-field Ising circuit and choose a single-qubit $Z$ observable on the middle qubit.\n"
msgstr "Pertama, bangun circuit Ising medan transversal dengan Trotterisasi 10 qubit dan pilih observable $Z$ satu qubit pada qubit tengah.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/quickstart/extracted-outputs/0fff4e37-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/quickstart/extracted-outputs/0fff4e37-1.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "SLC operates on the noisy two-qubit-gate layers of the circuit. Here we use ``samplomatic`` to group the gates into annotated boxes and attach a noise-injection annotation to each two-qubit layer. SLC requires every noisy box to have a unique `modifier_ref`, which `inject_noise_strategy=\"individual_modification\"` provides; with samplomatic's default strategy, the bounds come out wrong or their computation never finishes. `generate_noise_model_paulis` then enumerates the Pauli error terms of every unique noisy layer.\n"
msgstr "SLC beroperasi pada layer gate dua qubit yang berisik dari circuit. Di sini kita memakai ``samplomatic`` untuk mengelompokkan gate ke dalam kotak beranotasi dan memasang anotasi injeksi noise pada setiap layer dua qubit. SLC mensyaratkan setiap noisy box punya `modifier_ref` yang unik, yang disediakan oleh `inject_noise_strategy=\"individual_modification\"`; dengan strategi default samplomatic, bound yang dihasilkan salah atau perhitungannya tidak pernah selesai. `generate_noise_model_paulis` kemudian mengenumerasi suku error Pauli dari setiap layer berisik yang unik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Compute the shaded lightcone {#2-compute-the-shaded-lightcone}"
msgstr "2. Hitung shaded lightcone {#2-compute-the-shaded-lightcone}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The shaded lightcone is assembled by assigning a scale to each Pauli error term in the noise model based on how much effect it has on the observable expectation value. These scales are derived from each error term's forward and backward error bounds (described below), as well as its error rate:\n"
msgstr "Shaded lightcone dirakit dengan memberikan skala pada setiap suku error Pauli dalam model noise berdasarkan seberapa besar pengaruhnya terhadap nilai ekspektasi observable. Skala ini diturunkan dari bound error maju dan mundur setiap suku error (dijelaskan di bawah), serta tingkat error-nya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`compute_forward_bounds` evolves each error term *forward* to the end of the circuit to bound its effect on the observable measured there.\n"
msgstr "`compute_forward_bounds` mengevolusikan setiap suku error *maju* sampai akhir circuit untuk membatasi pengaruhnya terhadap observable yang diukur di sana.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`compute_backward_bounds` evolves each error term *backward* to the start of the circuit to bound its effect on the initial state.\n"
msgstr "`compute_backward_bounds` mengevolusikan setiap suku error *mundur* sampai awal circuit untuk membatasi pengaruhnya terhadap state awal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`merge_bounds` combines the two into a single bound per error term. Each bound is scaled by the term's error rate. These rates typically come from a noise learning experiment (such as `NoiseLearnerV3`); this guide uses random rates for simplicity.\n"
msgstr "`merge_bounds` menggabungkan keduanya menjadi satu bound per suku error. Setiap bound diskalakan dengan tingkat error suku tersebut. Tingkat ini biasanya berasal dari eksperimen pembelajaran noise (seperti `NoiseLearnerV3`); panduan ini memakai tingkat acak agar sederhana.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the shaded lightcone visualization below, each box is shaded by how strongly the errors at that site can affect the observable.  Bright boxes carry the largest bounds, while boxes that fade to the background contain error terms that have little effect on the calculation -- these errors are natural candidates to drop from the noise model. The values in the visualization below represent sums of the error bounds of all Pauli errors at that site, which is why some of the values grow larger than ``2.0``, the bound for any single Pauli error.\n"
msgstr "Pada visualisasi shaded lightcone di bawah, setiap kotak diberi warna sesuai seberapa kuat error di situs itu bisa memengaruhi observable.  Kotak yang terang membawa bound terbesar, sedangkan kotak yang memudar ke latar belakang berisi suku error yang pengaruhnya kecil terhadap perhitungan -- error ini kandidat alami untuk dibuang dari model noise. Nilai pada visualisasi di bawah mewakili jumlah bound error dari semua error Pauli di situs itu, itulah sebabnya beberapa nilai tumbuh lebih besar dari ``2.0``, yaitu bound untuk satu error Pauli tunggal.\n"

